  "query_preview": "(Sunday night through Thursday)...\nClouds will increase for Sunday night and Monday with a chance of showers\nfor late Sunday night and Monday. Through Monday afternoon, the chance \nfor 0.25 inch or more of rainfall remains below 25 percent.\n\nChances for rain will increase for Monday night as a strong Pacific storm \nmoves into southern California on Tuesday. It could bring heavy \nprecipitation, strong winds, high surf, and a chance of thunderstorms. \n\nThrough Wednesday night, the chance of 1 inch or more of rainfall\nexceeds 90 percent from the coast to the mountains. For Orange and \nsouthwestern San Bernardino Counties, the chance of 3 inches or more\nof rainfall ranges from 35 to 45 percent near the coast to 60 to 70\npercent in the mountains. For San Diego County, the chance for 3 inches\nor more of rainfall ranges from 40 to 50 percent over far northern\nportions of the county to 25 to 35 percent for far southern portions\nof the county. Through Tuesday, snow levels will mostly remain above \n8000 feet. Winds could strengthen to gale force over the coastal \nwaters on Tuesday.\n\nCurrent model timing would bring the most significant impacts into\nsouthwestern California around Tuesday morning. Precipitation\nwill continue through Tuesday night into Wednesday, then decrease\nfor Wednesday night and Thursday as the low pressure system moves\neastward and farther inland.",
